            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 68-year-old male admitted on 11/12/2023 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. He was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously throughout his stay. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Discharge was on 12/12/2023. I recommend continuation of his inhaled bronchodilator therapy and early pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Please arrange outpatient spirometry follow-up. Should you have any queries, please do not hesitate to contact me.</div>
               </text>
